+
+### Public file-offset ABI
+
+`MZ_FILE_OFFSET_BITS_64=ON` opts into `_FILE_OFFSET_BITS=64` for both the library
+and consumers on targets with POSIX headers and a 64-bit `off_t` in this mode.
+It is mutually exclusive with `MZ_FILE32_API=ON`; requesting both is an error.
+The option defaults to OFF and is not selected from the build machine's ABI.
+
+The definition is a public requirement of the CMake target `MINIZIP::minizip-ng`
+(or `MINIZIP::minizip` in compatibility mode) and the corresponding pkg-config
+module's `Cflags`. Consumers bypassing this metadata must define
+`_FILE_OFFSET_BITS=64` before including any system headers, in every translation
+unit using the library. Other definitions used internally remain private.
+
+On systems where this changes system type layouts, enabling the option is an
+ABI transition, not an ABI-neutral implementation change: `mz_os_read_dir`
+returns a system `struct dirent *`. Rebuild all consumers with the same mode;
+previously compiled narrow consumers are not made compatible by new metadata.
+Do not mix narrow and wide shared libraries with the same SONAME in a process.
+This option does not enable `_TIME_BITS=64`, which would also change public
+`time_t`-based APIs.
 
